pageType: content
background:
  type: solid
  color: "$bg"
elements:
  # ---------- header ----------
  - elementId: kicker
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 38, 700, 16]
    content:
      style: "$kicker"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        SOLUTION 1 OF 2 — SEMANTIC LAYER · A COMMON OBJECTION
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 58, 760, 44]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        Didn't the BI tool already do this?
  - elementId: title-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 118, 832, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}

  # ---------- column headers ----------
  - elementId: old-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [190, 136, 340, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$muted"
      bold: true
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        BI-tool semantic model — embedded
  - elementId: new-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [550, 136, 346, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 11.5
      color: "$sl"
      bold: true
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        Standalone semantic layer
  - elementId: head-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 160, 832, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}

  # ---------- row 1: storage ----------
  - elementId: r1-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 172, 110, 40]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      letterSpacing: 1.2
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        STORAGE
  - elementId: r1-old
    elementType: text
    bounds: [190, 170, 340, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$muted"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Definitions live inside the tool — Tableau calculated fields, Power BI measures, LookML</p>
  - elementId: r1-new
    elementType: text
    bounds: [550, 170, 346, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>A standalone definition layer — tool-agnostic, versioned, queryable by any consumer</p>
  - elementId: r1-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 232, 832, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}

  # ---------- row 2: access ----------
  - elementId: r2-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 246, 110, 40]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      letterSpacing: 1.2
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        ACCESS
  - elementId: r2-old
    elementType: text
    bounds: [190, 244, 340, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$muted"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Only that tool's users get the metric — everyone else rewrites it. Report C was exactly this</p>
  - elementId: r2-new
    elementType: text
    bounds: [550, 244, 346, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Dashboards, spreadsheets, notebooks, and AI agents all read the same definition</p>
  - elementId: r2-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 306, 832, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}

  # ---------- row 3: governance ----------
  - elementId: r3-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 320, 110, 40]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      letterSpacing: 1.2
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        GOVERNANCE
  - elementId: r3-old
    elementType: text
    bounds: [190, 318, 340, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$muted"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Wiki pages at best — the real definition lives in institutional memory</p>
  - elementId: r3-new
    elementType: text
    bounds: [550, 318, 346, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Definitions as code — every change tracked, reviewed, and auditable</p>
  - elementId: r3-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 380, 832, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}

  # ---------- row 4: flexibility ----------
  - elementId: r4-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 394, 110, 40]
    content:
      fontSize: 10
      color: "$muted"
      letterSpacing: 1.2
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        FLEXIBILITY
  - elementId: r4-old
    elementType: text
    bounds: [190, 392, 340, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$muted"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Changing a metric means editing the tool and re-testing its dashboards</p>
  - elementId: r4-new
    elementType: text
    bounds: [550, 392, 346, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 11
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Swap the BI tool or add a consumer — the certified definition stays constant</p>

  # ---------- takeaway ----------
  - elementId: takeaway-rule
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [64, 456, 832, 1]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$line"}
  - elementId: takeaway
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 470, 832, 30]
    content:
      fontSize: 12.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.4
      align: [left, top]
      text: |
        <p>Yes — the idea is old. What's new is <strong>where the definition lives</strong>: outside any single tool, so every consumer, human or AI, shares it.</p>

  # ---------- footer ----------
  - elementId: footer-left
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 514, 620, 14]
    content:
      style: "$caption"
      wrap: false
      align: [left, middle]
      text: |
        Note: embedded models like LookML are real semantic layers — the difference is coupling, not quality
  - elementId: footer-right
    elementType: text
    bounds: [830, 514, 66, 14]
    content:
      style: "$caption"
      wrap: false
      align: [right, middle]
      text: |
        03 / 05
